# Kokorev et al. (2024), ApJ 968, 38 (arXiv:2401.09981v4), Table 2: UV LF of photometrically selected little red dots (blank JWST fields)
# Redshift: 4.5 < z_phot < 6.5 (labelled <z> = 5 in the paper; mean z_phot of the LRDs in this bin = 5.3 from the Zenodo catalogue)
# Magnitude definition: observed (not dust-corrected) M_UV at rest-frame 1450 A, AGN and host not decomposed -> M1450
# Phi convention: log10(Phi / cMpc^-3 mag^-1) (H0=70), symmetric errors in dex
# Note: 5-sigma completeness limit M_UV ~ -18.5; the paper's Schechter fit uses only brighter bins (the -17 bin is incomplete).
# Note: the M_UV = -22 bin (N=1) is quoted as an upper limit (log Phi < -6.52) and is in Kokorev2024_ulimit.
#
# M1450  LogPhi  Delta
-17 -4.56 0.45
-18 -4.49 0.11
-19 -4.79 0.12
-20 -5.19 0.20
-21 -6.21 0.61
